<h3>Monitoring</h3>
<p><%= link_to "Preprocessing refresh policies", preprocessing_policies_path %> — explicit opt-in, separate from website schedules.</p>
<p><%= link_to "Open monitoring", monitoring_path(seedurl: "all") %> for blocked source fetches, flagged DSL errors, and enrolled preprocessing problems.</p>
<% if (website = transition_context_website) && !website.monitoring_excluded? %>
  <p>Website monitoring is <strong><%= website.monitorable? ? "on" : "off" %></strong> for <%= website.name %>.
    <%= link_to "Edit website monitoring", edit_website_path(website, anchor: "website-monitoring") %></p>
<% else %>
  <p>Enable source fetch alerts under Website monitoring in each website’s settings.</p>
<% end %>
<%= form_with model: @monitoring_setting, url: monitoring_options_path, method: :patch, local: true do |form| %>
  <%= form.label :mailbox, "Monitoring mailbox" %>
  <%= form.email_field :mailbox, placeholder: "monitoring@example.org" %>
  <%= form.check_box :weekly_pulse_enabled %>
  <%= form.label :weekly_pulse_enabled, "Send a weekly monitoring pulse, even with no open issues" %>
  <%= form.submit "Save monitoring settings" %>
<% end %>
<p>The optional daily digest lists open issues from Monitoring. Leave the mailbox blank to disable email.</p>
<p>The weekly pulse lists the same open issues as Monitoring. It replaces that day's error digest. Sent on the first scheduled run each week (Monday–Sunday, America/Toronto).</p>
<p>Last weekly pulse: <%= @monitoring_setting.last_pulse_week_on || "Not sent" %> (week starting Monday).</p>
<p>Last digest: <%= @monitoring_setting.last_digest_on || "Not sent" %> (America/Toronto).</p>
<% if ENV["MONITORING_EMAIL_FROM"].blank? %><p>Email setup required: sender and email delivery must be configured before sending.</p><% end %>
<details><summary>Flag a DSL error for monitoring</summary>
  <pre>['abort_update', { error: 'Audience mapping is stale', notify: 'daily' }]</pre>
  <p>Use this only for errors that need attention. Other errors retain their existing behavior. Email runs through the separately scheduled monitoring digest task.</p>
</details>
